            <ArticleTitle>[Latent endogenous depressions. I. Pseudoorganic neurosomatic symptomatology].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>857-62</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>On the basis of a clinical follow-up study of 384 patients with cyclothymia and schizophrenia with the picture of larvated depressions the author distinguishes 5 groups of somatovegetative sensations according to anatomo-physiological projections: cardiovascular (37%), neurological (32%), abdominal (23%), bone-muscular (5%), skin (3%). The traits of pathological sensations, imitating genuine somatoneurological pathology is discussed in a differential diagnostic aspect.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
